; Regression: a method named WITHOUT its tuple is the method, not a call
; (2026-10-04). The collapse used to append an empty
; tuple to a name whose last hop is a method -- `name.length` called -- and a
; thing that is not written shut out the method as a value. Twelve places in
; the compiler wrote it, all `String.length`; 25 794 write the `()`.
; Until a method is a value of its own the bare name is refused.
;
; xfail: 'length' is a method and stands here without its tuple

let name String("abc")
let n name.length
print "`n`\n"
